// An item's note put onto the line (N-101 post 406; the joint proposal's J, N-101 post 357). Where a project's notes lie
// in one of its repositories and it has a line, `coord item open` makes the note a commit on the line's head (branch
// note/ID, items.rs `item_opened`) and opens this under the item: the runner takes it as any hand-in, so the runner stays
// the one way onto the line. While the runner is down the step waits for it. Red (it could not go onto the line): raised,
// and the note stays on its branch.
/// an item's note put onto the line by the runner
kind note
  form commit: Ref
  result Ref
  raises NotOnLine
  pattern
    v <- step runner hand_in(commit);
    match v {
      OnLine(top) => return top
      Red(errors) => raise NotOnLine(errors)
    }
